acme_app_owner: hey team, high severity for us — since the runtime deploy on 2026-03-15 our consumer app sees constant parsing failures when using json_mode + streaming. pydantic errors out with ValidationError. repro and raw stream below, ticket https://support.example.com/t/4567

acme_app_owner: repro (minimal):
```bash
curl -N -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H \"Accept: text/event-stream\" -d '{\"model\":\"gpt-neoX-20B\",\"json_mode\":true,\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"generate order json\"}]}' https://api.redwood.example/v1/chat/completions
```

acme_app_owner: raw stream snippets we get (we concatenate data entries client-side):
```json
data: {"id":"resp_1","choices":[{"delta":{"content":"{\"order_id\":123,"}},"index":0}

data: {"id":"resp_1","choices":[{"delta":{"content":" \"status\": \"created\","}},"index":0}

data: [DONE]
```

acme_app_owner: when we join the chunks and run pydantic.parse_raw it throws: `ValidationError: Expecting value: line 1 column 1 (char 0)`. This only happens for a subset of responses (roughly 1/6).

julia_support: sorry about that — acking and triaging. can you confirm whether you see any 4xx/5xx from the API gateway or auth failures? also which SDK/lang are you using to assemble the SSE stream?

acme_app_owner: no 4xx/5xx, request returns 200 SSE stream. using node-fetch + eventsource-polyfill and we concat non-empty `data:` lines. sdk version: our client is homegrown.

sam_engineer: what likely happens: some SSE chunks include partial JSON or extra characters (heartbeats/empty data) that cause the simple concat to produce an invalid doc. two quick asks: (1) can you capture the exact raw bytes (including newlines) of the failing stream and paste (2) can you try `stream: false` to see if non-streaming avoids the issue?

acme_app_owner: pasted a raw dump in the ticket but here's a trimmed failing dump we captured (includes heartbeat):
```
data: {"id":"resp_1","choices":[{"delta":{"content":"{\"order_id\":123,\n"}},"index":0}

data: 

data: {"id":"resp_1","choices":[{"delta":{"content":" \"status\": \"created\"\n"}},"index":0}

data: [DONE]
```

acme_app_owner: note the isolated `data: ` empty heartbeat between chunks — our concat keeps it and ends up with `...123,\n\n \"status...` which trips pydantic.

zach_ml: good find. pydantic (and a strict json parser) will choke if there are stray newlines/empty lines that your concat doesn't strip. two options: client-side sanitize (ignore empty `data:` events, join with no extra newlines, trim) OR server-side: we can add a streaming sanitizer that filters empty heartbeat events and only emits `data: ` lines that contain non-whitespace before building the JSON object.

sam_engineer: quick workaround for node:
```js
let buffer = '';
function onData(line) {
  if (!line.trim()) return; // skip empty data
  buffer += line.replace(/^data:\s*/,'');
  try {
    const parsed = JSON.parse(buffer);
    // success -> emit and reset
    handle(parsed);
    buffer = '';
  } catch (e) {
    // incomplete, keep buffering
  }
}
```

sam_engineer: we should also instrument the runtime to avoid inserting extra blank `data:` events between JSON fragments. tagging eng-runtime. @ingress-bot can you pull the streaming proxy logs for 1816000000-1816004500 for streams to gpt-neoX-20B?

ingress-bot: logs pulled and attached to ticket 4567 (internal link). I see intermittent blank `data:` entries from the proxy at ~1816004325 and ~1816004358 correlating with the failing client dumps.

julia_support: escalation OK — marking as P1, adding eng-runtime owners. priority asks for us: (A) customer to try client-side sanitize or `stream:false` to confirm, (B) eng-runtime to add a short-term runtime filter to drop empty `data:` SSE lines, (C) we add a regression test that streams a JSON broken into odd chunk boundaries with blank heartbeats.

acme_app_owner: trying the node workaround now, I'll report back in ~10m. thanks for the quick triage :thumbsup:

sam_engineer: follow-up — for schema validation integrations (pydantic/jsonschema/zod) recommend clients validate after a full parse and allow recoverable parse errors by re-requesting the missing chunk. also adding note to docs: \"Streaming + json_mode: best practices for SSE parsing\".

acme_app_owner: quick update — workaround worked, no more parse errors after skipping blank data events and reassembling. leaving ticket open for runtime fix and docs.

julia_support: great, keeping ticket open and will post updates. thanks all.
